From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:27:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: provider allowlist, OpenRouter endpoint config, and
 auth selection

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Expose and enforce provider-family execution allowlist, generic OpenRouter endpoint config, OpenRouter reported cost accounting, and auth refresh preserving launch defaults
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 0004-privacy-improvements.patch
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 0006-provider-improvements.patch

Patch intent:
Add a provider-family execution allowlist that gates model switching,
persisted routes, dispatch, failover, and all direct memory-sidecar egress.
Empty or absent means unrestricted except for the hosted jcode provider (denied
unless explicitly listed); a non-empty list fails closed for unknown identities.
Picker-visibility methods also respect the allowlist so routes for denied
families are hidden.

Add `provider.openrouter_api_base` so the regular `openrouter` provider can
target any OpenRouter-compatible deployment, such as a regional endpoint,
without a separate provider identity. Precedence is
`JCODE_OPENROUTER_API_BASE`, then the config value, then the canonical
endpoint. The configured endpoint drives the runtime, the standard catalog
refresh, picker catalog acceptance, and usage key/credits probes. Request
OpenRouter SSE usage accounting (`usage.include = true`), emit terminal
provider-reported USD costs on `StreamEvent::ReportedCost`, and persist only
real reported costs as `StoredTokenUsage.cost_usd` while honoring explicit
`model_catalog = false` on named OpenRouter profiles. Auth refresh updates
runtime identity, credentials, and transport without changing startup selection
markers, so fresh sessions honor configured provider/model defaults unless an
explicit launch override selected a provider. OpenRouter runtimes carry an
immutable per-instance cache namespace used for model, endpoint, and pricing
caches.

Why it exists:
Keeps sessions inside explicit provider allowlists, including auxiliary
sidecar calls that would otherwise bypass main-provider dispatch, lets users
route OpenRouter traffic through a chosen deployment from shipped TOML config
while keeping one OpenRouter family, credential, and cache, and records real
provider-reported OpenRouter usage and USD cost without fabricating estimates.
Shared auth activation stops manufacturing explicit launch overrides that
previously suppressed configured new-session defaults.

Tests that register the process-global active provider could leak that
registration into later tests in the same process. A cfg(test)
ActiveProviderTestGuard RAII captures and clears the exact stored
registration and restores it on drop, including during unwinds, so guarded
tests get a deterministic provider state and clean up even when they fail.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-config-types/src/lib.rs adds allowed_providers,
openrouter_api_base, and tri-state NamedProviderConfig::model_catalog.
crates/jcode-provider-core/src/lib.rs defines ProviderFamily,
ProviderFamilyPolicy, RuntimeKey::route_id, and provider_family() methods on
RuntimeKey and ModelRouteApiMethod. crates/jcode-message-types/src/lib.rs and
crates/jcode-session-types/src/lib.rs add ReportedCost and StoredTokenUsage
cost_usd. crates/jcode-provider-openrouter/src/stream.rs parses usage.cost,
crates/jcode-provider-openrouter-runtime requests usage accounting and respects
model_catalog overrides, and crates/jcode-app-core persists terminal reported
cost on assistant messages. crates/jcode-base/src/provider/mod.rs, dispatch.rs,
multi_provider.rs, catalog_memo.rs, catalog_remote_routes.rs, catalog_routes.rs,
openrouter.rs, sidecar.rs, usage/provider_fetch.rs, and auth/lifecycle*.rs
enforce allowlists, endpoint config, and routing-neutral auth activation.

Update guidance:
Keep ProviderFamily taxonomy exhaustive and apply policy to all direct provider
clients. Keep the policy fail-closed for unknown entries and deny hosted jcode
by default unless listed. Keep ActiveProviderTestGuard cfg(test)-only.
Keep the OpenRouter endpoint generic and URL-free in Rust apart from the
canonical default. Preserve the override precedence, explicit `model_catalog =
false` disablement on named OpenRouter profiles, and terminal reported-cost
persistence without inventing fallback prices. Keep auth refresh independent of
initial CLI selection for every provider.

